<!-- @after 12. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- Remote payloads describe composition and content; native binaries own executable behavior.
- Negotiate component versions and validate props, unique IDs and fallback limits before composing.
- Cache raw payloads by owner, screen and server cache key; a segment is not an account boundary.
- Route only allowlisted actions and URIs, and make malformed sections fall back without poisoning the screen.
- Track each render separately and retain earlier-launch crash evidence until success, replacement or eviction; first-frame quarantine does not cover later lazy-section crashes.
